course: dictionary
lesson: 3333
title: Everything: a small word with a big job
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Everything» is a pronoun. A pronoun stands in for nouns, so you do not have to repeat them. It means all the things, every single thing: «Almost everything you touch was designed by someone.» Read it as: all the things you touch were designed by someone.
explain: «Everything» is one whole, so it takes a singular verb. We say «everything is fine», not «everything are fine». When you read it, check the verb after it, and see whether it is talking about all the things or one big idea.
explain: Sometimes «everything» means more than all the things. «My dog is everything to me» means my dog is the most important thing in my life. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning is meant.
fact: Everything means all the things, every single thing.
fact: Everything is a pronoun: it stands in place of nouns.
fact: Everything takes a singular verb: everything is, everything has.
fact: «Everything» can mean the most important thing, as in «my dog is everything to me».
fact: «Everything else» means all the rest, and «everything is fine» means nothing is wrong.
exercise: «Almost everything you touch was designed by someone.» What does everything mean here? | Only the road signs | Just the crisp bag | *All the things you touch | Only the chair you sit on
exercise: «In a fair test you change only one thing and keep everything else the same.» What does everything else mean? | Only the thing you changed | *All the other things, the rest | A brand-new test | The final result
exercise: Ella writes two sentences. Which one is correct? | Everything be ready for the trip | *Everything is ready for the trip | Everything are ready for the trip | Everything were ready for the trip
test: In «my dog is everything to me», what does everything mean? | Every single thing in the world | A dog food bowl | Lots of small things | *The most important thing in my life
test: Which sentence uses everything correctly? | Everything in the box are broken | Everything in the box be broken | *Everything in the box was broken | Everything in the box were broken
exam: The father told his son «everything I have is yours», so what does everything mean? | The celebration they shared | Nothing at all, because the father was poor | Only the father's old shoes | *All that I own and have
